+# Logistic twins: approved implementation contract
+
+Approved 6 October 2026 in the current Codex chat. Goal: repair the Julia fixed-effect logistic MLE and add native R Bernoulli-logit studies. Result is local, uncommitted review material. No commit, push, merge, installation, campaign, GLMM, LMM integration or publication.
+
+## Bases and preservation
+Julia base 9f0dd012f522b083a45ec03af7fad9bdbc9eb8e3; R base f44a0bfe29d34f081f7eaca3d07b0fbf93a3bf2f. The two exact fresh roots are recorded in .unlazy/logistic-twins/source/setup.json. Preserve the two canonical roots and the entire protected GroundTruth-lmm root, including docs/HANDOVER.md and R branding. Baseline file/status/diff hashes are .unlazy/logistic-twins/source/preservation-baseline.json. Never import whole dirty trees or old check wrappers.
+
+## Symbolic alignment
+Y_i ~ Bernoulli(p_i), logit(p_i)=alpha+beta*x_i. Numeric finite x and numeric y exactly 0/1; equal lengths n>2, unit weights, intercept plus one predictor. DGP: independently standard-normal x; Bernoulli y at declared probabilities. Fitters receive data without truth. Extractor maps intercept to alpha and slope to beta. Recovery compares these named log-odds coefficients. Logistic intervals are normal Wald at 0.90 and 0.95; Gaussian intervals stay Student t.
+
+## Exact finite-MLE diagnosis
+Reject all-zero/all-one outcomes and constant predictor with explicit messages. For response-class supports [a0,b0],[a1,b1], complete separation is b0<a1 or b1<a0; quasi separation is equality in either direction with predictor variation. Unique finite MLE requires b0>a1 and b1>a0. Exact comparisons, no support tolerance/jitter. Include singleton/tied finite-MLE case. Rounded fitted probabilities alone do not diagnose separation.
+
+## Julia numerical repair
+Keep logistic_mle signature, level=.95, maxiter=80, tol=1e-9 and FitResult schema. Validate controls. Use c=xmin/2+xmax/2, s=max(abs(x-c)), z=(x-c)/s; fit gamma0+gamma1*z. beta=gamma1/s; alpha=gamma0-c*beta. Finite large slopes are allowed; transformed nonfinite points fail explicitly.
+Stable loss is softplus((1-2*y)*eta); stable residual is sigmoid(-eta) for y=1 and -sigmoid(eta) for y=0. Stable weights exp(-abs(eta))/(1+exp(-abs(eta)))^2. Mean score g=Z'*(y-p)/n, mean information J=Z'*W*Z/n. Use PD factorization solve Delta=J\g. Start at zero. Armijo L(gamma+lambda*Delta)<=L(gamma)-1e-4*lambda*g'Delta; lambda starts 1, at most 40 halvings. Floating comparison allowance only 8eps(Float64)*max(1,abs(L)).
+Convergence after recomputation requires max(abs(g))<=tol, max(abs(Z*Delta))<=tol, g'Delta/2<=tol^2/2. A damped small step or small objective change alone is insufficient. maxiter=0 is an iteration-limit failure for finite-MLE data. Document new standardized interpretation of tol. Recompute final information; solve covariance and transform full matrix. Point failures reject all points; interval-only failures keep points and omit affected intervals, with explicit message. No FitResult diagnostics extension.
+
+## R interface and numerical contract
+Append gt_scenario family='gaussian', supporting gaussian/logistic only. sigma default lazily 1.2 for gaussian and NULL for logistic; explicit non-NULL sigma with logistic errors. Append gt_adapter family='gaussian'; familyless legacy objects default gaussian. Custom logistic fitters opt in. gt_adapter(fit=NULL,family='logistic') errors and directs to new gt_glm_adapter(id='glm',metadata=list()).
+Enforce family matches for all builtin and custom adapters before fit is called. Mismatch records existing fit_error and empty target rows, retaining denominator. Keep one-argument callback and fresh exactly x,y data.frame with no truth or family attribute injected.
+Native R standardized stats::glm(binomial/logit), na.fail, singular.ok=FALSE, epsilon=1e-12, maxit=200. Same exact existence checks. Require native convergence and independent standardized score/correction checks using tol=1e-9; no Julia polishing, no tolerance weakening. Stable final information yields 90/95 normal Wald intervals. Keep native vcov, warnings, iteration count, convergence and inference provenance separate in existing diagnostics. Declared inference is final-information Wald. Preserve accepted points on interval-only failure. Existing fit_error/nonconverged/invalid_estimate accounting remains.
+
+## Compatibility and exports
+Keep Gaussian x then error draw path, seed keys/collisions/canonical allocation, RNG kinds/restoration and groundtruth-r-rng-v1 unchanged. Preserve frozen Gaussian bytes and legacy Gaussian calls/objects. Observation table scenario,rep,row,x,y stays unchanged; targets alpha/beta and interval/status schemas stay unchanged.
+Export groundtruth-r-export-v2 records scenario family and adapter family; keep numeric sigma column with logistic NULL exported as missing numeric NA/empty CSV. Per-family provenance must be true. Preserve old v1 fixture files/manifests, no importer promised. R and Julia streams are distinct; parity uses identical frozen CSV bytes, never matching seed numbers. Refresh R implementation identity before tests/build.
+
+## Fixtures and frozen thresholds
+Reuse ten audit CSVs unchanged: retained,analytic,asymmetric,inverted,scaled,complete,quasi,all_zero,all_one,constant. Preserve original audit contract JSON as evidence of the earlier audit-only scope; this contract supplies new implementation authority. Add shifted analytic x'=3-100x; tied x=(-1,0,0,1),y=(0,0,1,0) with alpha=-log(3),beta=0; reflect separation deterministically; add independent fixed-point large-logit checks. Forced limits 0/1. Transform full covariance under shifts/reflections, including off-diagonal; reorder negative-scale slope endpoints. Do not add intercept interval endpoints separately.
+Ordinary coefficients/SE/endpoints atol=rtol=1e-7; information atol=1e-8,rtol=1e-7; mean NLL absolute 1e-10; original-fixture max absolute score 1e-7; analytic coefficient/SE absolute 1e-10,endpoints absolute 1e-9. No widening. Raw score threshold is an original-fixture oracle criterion, not unit-dependent runtime rule. Independent scalar oracle must not reuse production helpers.
+Controls reject swapped/missing/duplicate targets, sign flips, initial-information intervals, altered fixture bytes; harmless row permutation passes. Retain Gaussian wrong-normal-interval and SSE/n controls. Four-attempt accounting: 3 accepted estimates,2 usable intervals,conditional coverage 1/2,covered per attempt 1/4 for each target. Mixed-family study tests intended matches, mismatch failures and no fitter invocation on mismatch. Check replay/order/data isolation/RNG restoration, all-failed/singleton/zero-error summaries.
+
+## Evidence transport
+Each language writes .unlazy/logistic-twins/evidence/<julia|r>-fits.csv for shared comparison. Columns follow old audit r.csv: fixture,engine,status,target,estimate,se,lower90,upper90,lower95,upper95,nll,score_alpha,score_beta,Iaa,Iab,Ibb,message. Include original ten and shifted,tied; failure rows have alpha/beta target identities with empty numeric fields and explicit message. Point acceptance, interval usability and native-engine diagnostics are separately retained in language reports. Julia calls both levels independently, without runner schema expansion. Controls test candidate checker sensitivity; success markers only after assertions.
+
+## Phases, routing, time, gates
+Recon Luna low; parent contract/ledgers; one Sol high contract challenge and Julia core (load-bearing optimizer), R Luna medium; docs Luna medium. At most 3 workers plus parent; no nested delegation. Four producer roles, reuse for repairs; fresh completion panel 2 Luna medium+1 Sol high. Actual enforced CLI manifests required, no Astra/ultra. Expected engineering elapsed 4-6h. Local small numerical fits/loading allowance 15 minutes cumulative; each fitting command timeout no more remaining budget, record elapsed and stop/report overrun. JULIA_NUM_THREADS=1 and OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=1; no install or remote compute.
+Root gates G0 authorization; G1 environment/preservation; G2 red regression/fixture hashes; G3 paired independent science; G4 Gaussian/RNG/API/export compatibility; G5 accounting/controls; G6 package/docs; G7 fresh panel; G8 preservation/after-task/reconciliation. Before dispatch write root/leaf CHECK/EXPECT ledgers with disjoint OWNS. Inspect commands/scripts before --approve; exact cwd/shell/PATH/timeouts. --reverify before completion. Missing/abandoned gates prevent unqualified done.
+Finish: exact diffs, reproducible evidence/controls, package checks, rendered previews, fresh reviews, preservation receipts, after-task and plan-actual records. Local and uncommitted only. Tested fixed-effect numerical agreement, no calibration/mixed-model/package-wide parity claim. Commit/push/deploy require final approval of concrete bundle.
